  },
  {
   "text": "22 scenes",
   "start": 18.239,
   "duration": 16.698,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "24 packages",
   "start": 18.689,
   "duration": 16.248,
   "x": 560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Half the people who reviewed this free demo had already played it\nfor eleven hours. Not one of them quit inside ten minutes. Not one.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "duration": 8.3
  },
  {
   "text": "And the people leaving negative reviews had played\nlonger than the people leaving positive ones.",
   "start": 8.55,
   "duration": 4.539
  },
  {
   "text": "Guildrun is a PvE autobattler roguelike. You build a team, you bend\nheroes out of their class, and you watch the fight resolve itself.",
   "start": 16.939,
   "duration": 8.797
  },
  {
   "text": "Nearly two thousand reviews, ninety percent positive, and about two and a half\nthousand people in it as I record this. That's the biggest demo I've taken apart.",
   "start": 25.986,
   "duration": 8.901
  },
  {
   "text": "It's also the first one where the file list\ntold me the team had done this before.",
   "start": 35.137,
   "duration": 4.251
  },
  {
   "text": "Start with the awkward part. This is an I L two C P P build,\nso all the C sharp is fused into one Game Assembly file.",
   "start": 39.638,
   "duration": 7.83
  },
  {
   "text": "In the last teardown that was a dead end.\nThere's no folder of package names to read.",
   "start": 47.718,
   "duration": 5.218
  },
  {
   "text": "Except it isn't quite a dead end. Any assembly that shipped with embedded\nresources leaves its name behind in a data file, and Steam lists those.",
   "start": 53.186,
   "duration": 8.797
  },
  {
   "text": "Twenty four names came out. Here's what\na team that has shipped before installs.",
   "start": 62.233,
   "duration": 4.303
  },
  {
   "text": "Sentry, with six assemblies and a native crash handler behind it. They've shipped\na patch every single week since January. That's what makes that survivable.",
   "start": 66.786,
   "duration": 9.371
  },
  {
   "text": "S Q Lite, because the demo alone has three hundred relics and a\nhundred items. At some point that stops being a pile of JSON files.",
   "start": 76.407,
   "duration": 7.83
  },
  {
   "text": "N Log for structured logging. R three and System Reactive for\nevent streams. Threading Channels for the producer-consumer work.",
   "start": 84.487,
   "duration": 8.797
  },
  {
   "text": "And Z Link, which exists for one reason: doing LINQ without allocating.\nYou install that when you've been bitten by garbage collection hitches.",
   "start": 93.534,
   "duration": 7.961
  },
  {
   "text": "None of that is exciting. It's the stuff you only know to\ninstall because something went wrong on the last project.",
   "start": 101.745,
   "duration": 6.341
  },
  {
   "text": "Compare the solo demo I took apart two episodes ago. Its\nentire third party list was one entry: Discord rich presence.",
   "start": 108.336,
   "duration": 8.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Neither is wrong. But if you're about to start your\nsecond project, that list up there is a shopping list.",
   "start": 116.886,
   "duration": 6.289
  },
  {
   "text": "Audio is F MOD with Resonance, same as the last\none. Networking is nanosockets, a thin U D P layer.",
   "start": 123.425,
   "duration": 7.595
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the number I\nstared at for a while.",
   "start": 131.27,
   "duration": 2.397
  },
  {
   "text": "The demo is ten and a half gigabytes on\ndisk. The download is one point one seven.",
   "start": 133.917,
   "duration": 5.035
  },
  {
   "text": "That's an eighty nine percent saving. Which means the\nfiles sitting on your drive are barely compressed at all.",
   "start": 139.202,
   "duration": 6.028
  },
  {
   "text": "My first thought was that somebody forgot the import\nsettings. My second thought was to read the store page.",
   "start": 145.48,
   "duration": 6.054
  },
  {
   "text": "Minimum requirements: fifteen gigabytes of storage,\nand a line that says H D D okay, no S S D required.",
   "start": 151.784,
   "duration": 7.517
  },
  {
   "text": "Uncompressed assets cost disk and save C P U. On a hard drive with no\ndecompression to do, they load faster. My read is that this is deliberate.",
   "start": 159.551,
   "duration": 9.371
  },
  {
   "text": "They spent ten gigabytes of somebody's drive to keep the game playable\non old hardware. Tell me in the comments if I've got that backwards.",
   "start": 169.172,
   "duration": 7.177
  },
  {
   "text": "There are also twenty two scenes in here. The last two games I took apart shipped\none each and built everything at runtime. This one is authored in the editor.",
   "start": 176.599,
   "duration": 8.666
  },
  {
   "text": "So the engineering is careful. The fight in\nthe reviews is about something else entirely.",
   "start": 185.515,
   "duration": 5.192
  },
  {
   "text": "Performance barely comes up. Ten mentions positive,\ntwo negative. Nobody is complaining about the build.",
   "start": 190.957,
   "duration": 6.21
  },
  {
   "text": "They're complaining about balance. Certain combinations only, dead\nheroes, and a random draw that decides your run before you play it.",
   "start": 197.417,
   "duration": 7.83
  },
  {
   "text": "And that's why the negative reviewers had fifteen hours in. You don't find\na balance ceiling in an hour. You find it after you've mastered the thing.",
   "start": 205.497,
   "duration": 7.83
  },
  {
   "text": "Which is a very different problem from the\ndemos where people quit in the first hour.",
   "start": 213.577,
   "duration": 4.121
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the whole\nteardown on one card.",
   "start": 217.948,
   "duration": 2.292
  },
  {
   "text": "Unity, I L two C P P, C sharp. A stack full of things you only reach for\nthe second time around. Ten gigabytes of deliberately uncompressed art.",
   "start": 220.49,
   "duration": 10.024
  },
  {
   "text": "Worth a dip, and be careful,\nbecause eleven hours is the median.",
   "start": 230.764,
   "duration": 4.251
  },
  {
   "text": "If you're starting your next project, take the boring half of that list.\nCrash reporting on day one is the cheapest thing you will ever install.",
   "start": 235.265,
   "duration": 7.83
  },
  {
   "text": "That's my read from the outside. If you made this and I got something wrong, say so and\nI'll pin the correction. Next time, another demo, another file list. This is Demo Dip.",
   "start": 243.345,
   "duration": 10.233
  }
 ],
